  "rules": {
    "oneOwnerPerRoute": "Every row names exactly one production-capable deletion owner (ENCL0 or ENCF0), or names no deletion owner because it is an accepted Rev11 surface that ENCT0 verifies, or a recorded retained/unused item.",
    "inheritedRoutes": "parentRoute names the UAK0 route a row splits (D16 for non-editor public positions, D17 for editor contracts). The parent keeps its owner; the row only narrows it. parentRoute null marks a route UAK0 did not list.",
    "productionCapable": "ENCT0, ENC1 and UAI0 delete nothing and are never deletion owners here.",
    "identifiable": "identifiable=false marks a wire whose encoding a consumer cannot determine from the wire, its type or its fixed contract. Each such row has abortEvidence=true: it triggers the charter clause 'abort if a current wire cannot identify its encoding'.",
    "excluded": "Test-only conversions, tooling crates outside the production closure (verter_bench examples, verter_dx_baseline, lsp-test-client) and JS-internal string indices that never cross a Rust boundary (unplugin ssr-transforms) are outside the population."
